# Jaguar 240 four-door saloon, 1967-1969.
#
# The final 2.4-litre Mark 2 derivative: slim chrome bumpers, a revised grille
# and the Ambla-trimmed interior of the 1967 range. It is the Mark 2 shell with
# the later detailing, not a new body.
# https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jaguar_Mark_2
#
# Dimensions 4.57 x 1.70 x 1.47 m, wheelbase 2.72 m.
#
# Shape reference: a near-profile about 5-10 degrees off perpendicular, plus
# front and rear three-quarters. It is close to a true side and is the best
# available; the small angle is recorded.
#
# Colours: grade (d); no UK brochure was consulted. British Racing Green,
# Black, Old English White and Carmen Red are period Jaguar finishes. Weights 3,
# 2, 2, 1, total 8, provisional pending the central rebase.
#
# Speed 170 km/h. Comfort 75/443, on the line 330 + 1.5 x 75. Classes 2,3.
# Dates 1967-1969 production, road tail staggered 1982-1984.
#
# Metres master: citycars/4.5/jaguar-240.blend. Interchange:
# citycars/4.5/jaguar-240.dae. References: citycars/references/jaguar-240/
# (gitignored; Wikimedia Commons).
#
# Accepted deviations: the shell was corrected in a derivative copy because the
# existing Mark 2 master's squared nose and angular roof/rear glazing did not
# match the photographs. The existing Mark 2 asset is left untouched. The side
# reference is a near-profile 5-10 degrees off, not a true elevation.


obj=citycar
